var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#Corset.jl","page":"Home","text":"Corset turns code-quality rules into tests. A rule is a function that reads a loaded module (its lowered and inferred code, bindings and types) or a source file, and returns the places where the code breaks it. ratchet! turns those places into one @test.\n\nCorset checks things a linter cannot see because they need the compiler's answer: a local variable that infers as Any, a closure that boxes a captured variable, a function that reads a mutable global, a Float32 kernel that computes in Float64.","title":"Corset.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Install","page":"Home","text":"pkg> add Corset","title":"Install"},{"category":"section","location":"#A-first-check","page":"Home","text":"Write a module with two problems.\n\nmodule Demo\nconst COUNTER = Ref(0)\nbump(x) = x + COUNTER[]\n\nfunction total(xs)\n    acc = 0\n    for x in xs\n        acc += x / 2\n    end\n    acc\nend\nend\n\nbump reads a mutable global, so its result depends on state its signature does not show. In total, acc starts as an Int and becomes a Float64, so the compiler infers a union for it. Ask Corset for the offenders of the two rules that notice this:\n\nrepo = Repository(root)\noffenders!(repo, \"hidden-input\", hidden_inputs(Demo))\n1-element Vector{String}:\n \"COUNTER\"\n\noffenders!(repo, \"abstract-local\", abstract_locals(repo, inferred_methods(Demo, [Tuple{typeof(Demo.total), Vector{Int}}])))\nString[]\n\nEach returned string is a key: the name of one offender. offenders! returns the keys and logs them; ratchet! does the same and fails a test if there are any.","title":"A first check"},{"category":"section","location":"#In-a-test-suite","page":"Home","text":"using Test\nusing Corset: Repository, ratchet!, hidden_inputs, abstract_locals, inferred_methods\nusing MyPackage\n\nconst REPO = Repository(pkgdir(MyPackage))\n\n@testset \"code rules\" begin\n    ratchet!(REPO, \"hidden-input\", hidden_inputs(MyPackage))\n    ratchet!(REPO, \"abstract-local\", abstract_locals(REPO, inferred_methods(MyPackage, SIGNATURES)))\nend\n\nWith no further setup every offender fails. A package with existing offenders adopts Corset one rule at a time through a baseline.","title":"In a test suite"},{"category":"section","location":"#Where-to-go-next","page":"Home","text":"Guide: wiring rules into runtests.jl, baselines, exemptions and opt-out comments.\nRules: every rule, what it finds and how to repair an offender.\nAPI: the exported names. The internals pages hold every other docstring.","title":"Where to go next"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"The exported names. The internals pages document the rest, grouped by the code each part reads.","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#Corset.Corset","page":"API","text":"Code-quality rules checked on a loaded module and on its repository's Julia source. A rule is a function returning the Sites it finds; ratchet! fails a test on them. By default every site fails; a Repository given a baseline file holds each rule to its per-rule counts there instead, failing on new offenders and lowering the counts when offenders go away. The caller picks the rules, the module and source files they read, and their limits.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Corset"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#Corset.Repository","page":"API","text":"Repository(root; baseline = nothing, one_letter_exempt = (), skipped_directories = (), file_line_limit = 1500)\n\nThe tree the rules read, and the settings that relax them. The defaults are the strict reading: every finding of every rule fails. root is the tree whose source the rules read (made absolute).\n\nbaseline: the TOML file of per-rule allowances that ratchet! holds findings to; nothing allows none. It may be a link: ratchet! resolves it at each call, so a lowering lands in the file it points to.\none_letter_exempt: the variable names the one-letter rule allows besides _ (a project's own convention, such as an argument everywhere named p).\nskipped_directories: directory names repository_sources leaves out wherever they sit, such as (\"vendor\",). Hidden directories (a leading .) are always left out.\nfile_line_limit: the most lines a source file may hold before the file-length rule reports it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Repository"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#Corset.Site","page":"API","text":"One offender a rule found: key names it in the baseline; file (a path, empty when the offender has none) and the lines line through last_line place it for the opt-out comments, so a comment on any of them takes the site out. Line 0 places it in the file as a whole. detail tells the reader of the log what the offender is (a variable and its type, say); a rule with nothing to add passes \"\", and the constructors have no default so no rule forgets it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Site"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#Corset.float64_ops-Tuple{Any, Tuple}","page":"API","text":"float64_ops(f, types)\n\nNumber of Float64 operations in the fully optimized IR of f(::types...).\n\nA wrapper number type observes a Float64 only when it is promoted with, or converted from, a wrapped number, so a dependency that computes internally at Float64 and narrows before returning is invisible to it — the expensive silent case, where the caller pays Float64 arithmetic and keeps Float32 storage. The IR sees that widening whichever package caused it, without forking or instrumenting the dependency.\n\nHeuristic, not a proof: it reads the IR optimize=true produced for one concrete signature, so a Float64 reached only through runtime dispatch is out of scope, and a non-inlined callee is visible through its call signature rather than its body. Use == 0 on kernels that must stay narrow, and keep the positive controls so a change to the filter cannot quietly disarm the check.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.float64_ops"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#Corset.offenders!-Tuple{Repository, String, AbstractVector{Site}}","page":"API","text":"offenders!(repository, rule, sites; scopes = (\"\",), fix = \"\")\n\nThe keys of rule's offenders sites that repository does not allow, logged. Sites that a # lint: comment naming the rule opts out are dropped and counted in the log; the rest are tallied by key. Without a baseline (Repository's default) every key is returned. With one, the offenders are held to rule's table in the baseline file: the keys past their entry are returned, and an entry the tally undercuts is lowered or deleted and the file rewritten. A rule with no table is seeded with its tally. Several testsets may share one rule's table, and a run may not measure all of it (a partial copy of the tree): each passes the prefixes scopes that begin the keys it measures, and only entries under one of them can fall. fix tells the reader of the log how to repair an offender, such as the forms the rule accepts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.offenders!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#Corset.ratchet!-Tuple{Repository, String, AbstractVector{Site}}","page":"API","text":"ratchet!(repository, rule, sites; scopes = (\"\",), fix = \"\")\n\nA test that rule's offenders sites are all allowed: it fails on the keys offenders! returns, and returns them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ratchet!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#Corset.undefined_names-Tuple{Any}","page":"API","text":"undefined_names(path; scope)\n\nScan one test file for names its testsets use but nothing defines.\n\nA name counts as defined when any binding of it appears anywhere in the file or its literal includes (every scope, including modules and other testsets): the scan over-approximates, so a reported name has no definition in reach.\n\nReturns (unresolved, unlowered). unresolved holds one \"line N:name\" entry per undefined name. unlowered names the testsets whose macros could not be expanded here, which the scan therefore did not cover: report it, because a scan that quietly skips a testset reads exactly like one that cleared it.\n\nscope is the module the testsets run in, which owns the macros the bodies use and the names they resolve against. Pass @__MODULE__.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.undefined_names"},{"category":"macro","location":"api/#Corset.@call_sites-Tuple{Any, Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"API","text":"@call_sites scope sites target_modules = (…,) call(…): JET.@report_call's reports appended to the vector sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.@call_sites"},{"category":"macro","location":"api/#Corset.@opt_sites-Tuple{Any, Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"API","text":"@opt_sites scope sites target_modules = (…,) call(…): JET.@report_opt's reports appended to the vector sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.@opt_sites"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/source/#Source-rules","page":"Source rules","text":"Rules that read parsed source files, and the rule registry.","title":"Source rules"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/source/#Corset.CONCRETE_RETURN_FIX","page":"Source rules","text":"The repair ratchet!'s fix names for a concrete_returns offender: the result annotations the rule accepts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.CONCRETE_RETURN_FIX"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/source/#Corset.Inferred","page":"Source rules","text":"A method typed over one signature by a single inference: its unoptimized typed code (named slots and their types), the optimized IRCode the optimizer makes of it, and whether inference found its return type to be Nothing (after widening, so a constant result nothing counts).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Inferred"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/source/#Corset.Located","page":"Source rules","text":"One expression of parsed source: line is the nearest line marker before it, enclosing the function definition it sits in (<top level> outside any) and enclosing_line that definition's line.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Located"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.abstract_declaration-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether field type declared is abstract: not a type parameter, not a Union, and holds_abstract.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.abstract_declaration"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.abstract_fields-Tuple{DataType}","page":"Source rules","text":"Fields of type declared with an abstract type (not a type parameter, not a Union), or with a concrete container of one: Vector{Any}, Base.RefValue{Any} and Dict{Tuple, Any} are concrete, but every read from them is dynamically dispatched.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.abstract_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.abstract_local_sites-Tuple{Corset.Inferred}","page":"Source rules","text":"The abstract_locals sites of item, one per abstract named local.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.abstract_local_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.abstract_local_type-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether inferred type inferred leaves the compiler without a concrete layout: abstract, a Union of more than UNION_SPLIT_LIMIT types or of any abstract one, or a collection or tuple that holds such elements (Vector{Any}). Type{X} is a value; a local never assigned (Union{}) holds nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.abstract_local_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.abstract_locals-Tuple{Repository, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Each named local variable (not an argument) of repository's own methods whose inferred type is abstract_local_type, one site per variable however many specializations ran. A method a macro generated in another package's file (@concrete's constructors) and a compiler's unnamed slot are not the repository's variables. An opt-out on a method's first line covers all its locals (audited_frames).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.abstract_locals"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.abstract_slot-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, AbstractSet{Int64}, Integer, Symbol, Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether slot index of item, named name and inferred type, is a named local (not an argument nor caught) of abstract_local_type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.abstract_slot"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.annotated_arguments-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"Each annotated argument below parsed argument, as its name (:_ when unnamed) and annotation, positional or keyword.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.annotated_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.anonymous_function_sites-Tuple{Module, Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"Each live_closure_types closure of mod with a fault of kind kind (closure_faults), as a closure_site whose detail is the fault. A closure that captures nothing, like x -> x.field, passes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.anonymous_function_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.bound_name-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"The variable a where clause entry binds: T, T <: Real or T >: Int.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.bound_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.bound_names-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"Each variable name a parsed target binds: an assignment target, a lambda or method parameter list, with its annotations, defaults and splats removed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.bound_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.c_type_sites-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"The C-interop type names (C_TYPE_NAMES) of the Julia file path outside a C call, by name_sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.c_type_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.called_type-Tuple{Type}","page":"Source rules","text":"The type a lowered statement names through binding value: the type itself, or a function instance's type (a keyword body).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.called_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.callee_name-Tuple{Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"The name of the type whose instances method is called on (its function's type), or nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.callee_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.calls_argument-Tuple{Expr, AbstractUnitRange}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether statement statement calls one of the arguments arguments (slot numbers) of its method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.calls_argument"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.capture_detail-Tuple{Symbol, Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"What a capture of type capture with fault kind (capture_kind) costs, for the site's detail.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.capture_detail"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.capture_kind-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"The kind of fault a capture of type capture is, in a compiled closure instance: :plain for plain_capture data, :overspecialized for a type or function (one compile per value), :impure for other concrete data (mutable state or a module), :unstable for a type inference left abstract.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.capture_kind"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.caught_slots-Tuple{Core.CodeInfo}","page":"Source rules","text":"The slots of code that a catch binds, which Julia always types Any.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.caught_slots"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.closure_definer-Tuple{Core.TypeName, AbstractDict{Core.TypeName, Method}}","page":"Source rules","text":"The method that creates closure type name: its namer in namers (closure_namers), followed out of nested closures to the first namer that is not itself a closure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.closure_definer"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.closure_faults-Tuple{DataType, Integer}","page":"Source rules","text":"The faults of closure type, as kind => detail pairs: a Core.Box or no compiled instance (its captures unverified) is :impure; otherwise the instance_faults of every instance. None for a closure that captures nothing, or only plain_capture data in every instance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.closure_faults"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.closure_instances-Tuple{DataType, Integer}","page":"Source rules","text":"The closure types Base.specializations records for the call methods of closure type: one per instance the package compiled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.closure_instances"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.closure_namers-Tuple{Module, AbstractVector{Method}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Each closure type that the lowered code of methods names, with a method that names it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.closure_namers"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.closure_site-Tuple{DataType, Method, Integer, AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"closure_site(type, definer, world, detail)\n\nThe site of closure type type, created by method definer (closure_definer), keyed by definer's file and name (method_key) because closure type names carry compiler counters. It sits at the closure's call method, or at definer when that method has no source file (code built without line numbers).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.closure_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.closure_type_names-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"The names of every is_unnamed_function_type bound in mod, live or left over.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.closure_type_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.concrete_arguments-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{Corset.Located}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Arguments annotated with a concrete container (is_concrete_container) that the method does not resize, one site per argument at the method's signature, keyed by file: AbstractVector{T} takes a view, an OffsetArray or a GPU array, a Vector{T} takes none of them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.concrete_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.concrete_returns-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{Corset.Located}, Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Methods whose declared return type names a concrete type (names_concrete_type), one site per method at its signature, keyed by file and function name: a result type must be generic, annotated by what the arguments bind, not by a fixed type. A package struct parameterized by the method's where variables is generic. A constructor returning its own struct (constructs_own_type) is exempt.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.concrete_returns"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.constructs_own_type-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether method definition node is a constructor: it is named for the type its return annotation names, Foo(…)::Foo or Foo{T}(…)::Foo{T}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.constructs_own_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.created_closures-Tuple{Method, Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Closure types (by name) that the lowered code of method creates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.created_closures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.defined_name-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"The name a parsed function definition node defines, or nothing when node defines none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.defined_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.definition_line-Tuple{Expr, Int64}","page":"Source rules","text":"The line a function definition node starts on: its body's first line marker, which Meta.parseall sets to the function line even after a docstring.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.definition_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.definition_lines-Tuple{Expr, Int64}","page":"Source rules","text":"The lines of function definition node's signature: from definition_line to the line before its body's first statement (one line for f(x) = …).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.definition_lines"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.definition_site-Tuple{AbstractString, Corset.Located}","page":"Source rules","text":"A Site at the definition lines of item.node in path, keyed by file basename and defined name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.definition_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.fatou_site-Tuple{AbstractString, RegexMatch}","page":"Source rules","text":"The site of found, a FATOU_FINDING match, in the repository at root.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fatou_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.fatou_sites-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Source rules","text":"One site per finding of fatou lint over directories of repository, keyed by file and Fatou rule and placed at the finding's line (the fatou rule's opt-out comment takes it out). Fatou must be installed; a run that prints a line it did not mean as a finding (a parse error) throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fatou_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.field_types-Tuple{DataType}","page":"Source rules","text":"The declared field types of type, type variables included.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.field_types"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.first_word-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"First word of a name in snake case: SolverControls and solver_tolerance both give \"solver\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.first_word"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.fixed_reach-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Set{T}, AbstractDict{T, Set{T}}}} where T","page":"Source rules","text":"live closed under created: every closure a member's own code creates, repeated until none is new.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fixed_reach"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.float64_sites!-Tuple{AbstractVector{Site}, AbstractString, Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Source rules","text":"Float64 tokens below syntax node, one site each at the token's own line, keyed by file: an untyped float literal, Float64, ComplexF64, or the constants Inf and NaN (also Inf64, NaN64). A field name (Base.Inf), a quoted symbol and an @changeprecision body, which parses at its own precision, are skipped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.float64_sites!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.float64_sites-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"The Float64 sites of the Julia file path, by float64_sites!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.float64_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.function_owner-Tuple{Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"The module that owns the function method is a method of.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.function_owner"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.global_reads-Tuple{GlobalRef}","page":"Source rules","text":"Every global node, a lowered statement, reads.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.global_reads"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.hidden_inputs-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"hidden_inputs(mod)\n\nEach read of a global that some method of mod takes besides its arguments and immutable constants, keyed by the global and placed at the statement that reads it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.hidden_inputs"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.holds_abstract-Tuple{Type}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether declared is abstract or has an abstract type among its parameters, at any depth. Allowed: Unions (small, split by the compiler), Type{T}, a struct's own type parameters (Vector{E} with E free), and value parameters (SVector{16, E}'s Tuple{16}).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.holds_abstract"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.impure_anonymous_functions-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Anonymous functions of mod that capture mutable state, hold a Core.Box, or were never compiled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.impure_anonymous_functions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.inferred_methods-Tuple{Module, AbstractVector{<:Type}}","page":"Source rules","text":"inferred_methods(mod, signatures)\ninferred_methods(mod, frames)\n\nEach method mod defines (methods it adds to another module's function included) that inference reaches from signatures, typed over each signature that selects it; the result depends on signatures alone. Given the frames of entry_frames, it filters them and infers nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.inferred_methods"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.instance_callees-Tuple{Core.MethodMatch}","page":"Source rules","text":"The function type each specialization of match's method was compiled for.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.instance_callees"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.instance_faults-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"The faults of closure instance instance, as kind => detail pairs (capture_kind, capture_detail).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.instance_faults"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_closure_type-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"is_closure_type(value)\n\nWhether binding value is a lowered anonymous function, do block or inner function (its type name starts with #).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_closure_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_concrete_container-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether parsed type expression annotation is a concrete container (Vector, Matrix, Array, Dict, bare or with parameters), alone or as a direct member of a Union.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_concrete_container"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_definition-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Definitions, not state: a DataType is itself ismutable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_definition"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_hidden_input-Tuple{GlobalRef}","page":"Source rules","text":"is_hidden_input(binding)\n\nWhether reading the global binding reads something besides an immutable constant: a non-constant binding, a mutable value (a Ref, Dict, cache, Array, Atomic), or a ScopedValue, whose value depends on the caller's scope rather than the arguments. Strings, symbols and regexes are immutable in use.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_hidden_input"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_one_letter-Tuple{Symbol, Tuple{Vararg{Symbol}}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether name is one letter long and not among the names exempt allows or _, which binds nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_one_letter"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_range_guard-Tuple{Real}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether parsed source node itself is an overflow or underflow guard: a call to floatmin or floatmax, a literal at the edge of exp's range, or isfinite of an expression calling exp.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_range_guard"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_struct_binding-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether binding value is a struct type, closures excluded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_struct_binding"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_unmarked_effect-Tuple{Repository, Corset.Inferred}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether item is an is_unmarked_function that inference types as always returning nothing: it exists for its effect, so its name says so. A method returning a call to its argument (returns_argument_call) gets no verdict: its callers' arguments decide its result.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_unmarked_effect"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_unmarked_function-Tuple{Repository, Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"An is_unmarked_method of a function its own module owns: not a method added to another package's function (Base.show).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_unmarked_function"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_unmarked_method-Tuple{Repository, Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether method is a method of repository for a named function whose name has no !, whoever owns the function (Base.length counts): not a closure, a constructor or a keyword call. __init__ is exempt, since Julia fixes its name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_unmarked_method"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.is_unnamed_function_type-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether binding value is the type of a closure, do block, inner or anonymous function: an is_closure_type that is not the type of a function named in source. Julia 1.12 binds a named function's type too (#add_slope! beside add_slope!), and code reaches that function through its name, not its type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_unnamed_function_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.jscpd_command-Tuple{AbstractString, Repository, AbstractVector{String}, AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"The Cmd running jscpd against dirs with report written to report_dir.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.jscpd_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.jscpd_site-Tuple{Repository, AbstractDict}","page":"Source rules","text":"One Site from duplicate, an item of a jscpd --absolute JSON report on repository.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.jscpd_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.jscpd_sites-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Source rules","text":"One site per duplicate code block found by jscpd over directories of repository, keyed by the duplicate file and the duplicated file, placed at the duplicate block's lines. jscpd must be installed and on PATH; an execution failure throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.jscpd_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.kind_detail-Tuple{AbstractVector{Pair{Symbol, String}}, Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"The details of the faults (closure_faults) of kind kind, joined; empty when there are none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.kind_detail"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.lacks_annotation-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether method definition node has an argument with no annotation or declares no return type; false for anything that is not a method definition.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.lacks_annotation"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.live_closure_types-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"The closure types the current code of mod can create (live_closures), unwrapped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.live_closure_types"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.live_closures-Tuple{Module, AbstractVector{Method}}","page":"Source rules","text":"live_closures(mod, methods)\n\nThe closure types (by name) that the current code of methods can create: those the lowered code of a method that is not itself a closure names, and those a live closure's own code names. A closure whose defining method was redefined in this process (by Revise, in a worker reused across trees) is a leftover type that no current code reaches, and is not the source's.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.live_closures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.locate!-Tuple{Vector{Corset.Located}, Expr, Int64, Symbol, Int64}","page":"Source rules","text":"Every expression below parsed source node, each as a Located; returns the line the walk ended on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.locate!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.located_source-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"Every expression of the parsed file path, as Locateds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.located_source"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.long_file_sites-Tuple{Repository, AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"A site for the file path as a whole (line 0) when it holds more than repository.file_line_limit lines, its count in the detail; none otherwise. A long file hides its structure; split it by topic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.long_file_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.lowered-Tuple{Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"Lowered code of method, or nothing for a generated or builtin method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.lowered"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.mentions_nothing-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether parsed type expression annotation is a Union with Nothing among its members.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.mentions_nothing"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.mentions_variable-Tuple{Symbol, Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether parsed type expression parameter mentions one of the type variables variables, at any depth.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.mentions_variable"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.method_hidden_inputs-Tuple{Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"The hidden_inputs sites of method's lowered code; none for a method without one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.method_hidden_inputs"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.method_key-Tuple{Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"The key an offender of a method goes under: its file and name, the file and \"anonymous function\" for a closure (whose name carries compiler counters).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.method_key"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.method_namings-Tuple{Method, Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Each closure type method's lowered code names (created_closures), paired with method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.method_namings"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.missing_annotations-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{Corset.Located}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Methods that lack an argument annotation or a return type, one site per method at its signature, keyed by file and function name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.missing_annotations"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.module_frames-Tuple{Module, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Source rules","text":"The frames whose method mod defines, on its own function or on another module's (Base.show).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.module_frames"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.module_methods-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"module_methods(mod)\n\nThe defined_methods of mod that its current code reaches: every method except a closure's that is not live_closures.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.module_methods"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.module_structs-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Struct types mod defines, closures excluded; a type bound to two names counts once.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.module_structs"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.mutable_structs-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"The module_structs of mod declared mutable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.mutable_structs"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.name_sites-Tuple{AbstractString, Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode, Tuple{Vararg{Symbol}}, Bool}","page":"Source rules","text":"Identifiers in syntax node named in names, one site each at the name's own line, keyed by file, outside the body of ccall, @ccall, cfunction, @cfunction and @ccallable (also written Base.ccall). A quoted symbol is skipped; so is a field name (Base.Cint) unless fields is set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.name_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.named_closures-Tuple{Core.CodeInfo, Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"The closure types of mod that lowered statements code name, by type name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.named_closures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.names_closure-Tuple{GlobalRef, Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether global read names an is_unnamed_function_type of mod.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.names_closure"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/source/#Corset.names_concrete_type","page":"Source rules","text":"names_concrete_type(annotation, scope, variables = ())\n\nWhether parsed type expression annotation names a concrete type of scope or of Base (Float32, Vector{E}, a package struct), alone or as a member of a Union. A result type must be generic (typeof(x), a type variable, AbstractVector{E}), so a fixed concrete type is named here, except Nothing, Bool, tuples and NamedTuples (EXEMPT_RESULT_TYPES) and enum types. A type variable, typeof(x) and an abstract type name none. A package struct with a parameter that mentions one of the method's where variables (Result{E}, Result{Vector{E}}) is generic too: it has no abstract form to name instead. Base's own concrete types stay concrete with such a parameter, since AbstractVector{E} names Vector{E}'s.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.names_concrete_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.nothing_returns-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{Corset.Located}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Functions declaring a Union{Nothing, …} return: a \"can't compute here\" answer, one site per definition.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.nothing_returns"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.one_letter_item_sites-Tuple{AbstractString, Corset.Located, Tuple{Vararg{Symbol}}}","page":"Source rules","text":"One site per one_letter_names name item of the file path binds, at the item's line or its definition's.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.one_letter_item_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.one_letter_names-Tuple{Expr, Tuple{Vararg{Symbol}}}","page":"Source rules","text":"The one-letter variable names parsed expression node itself binds, besides those exempt allows: method parameters, an assignment or loop target, a lambda parameter, a catch variable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.one_letter_names"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/source/#Corset.one_letter_sites","page":"Source rules","text":"One site per one-letter variable name in the Julia file path, keyed by file and enclosing function (or testset); repository.one_letter_exempt names the allowed ones.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.one_letter_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.one_per_line-Tuple{AbstractVector{Site}}","page":"Source rules","text":"One site per key, file and lines of sites, in first-seen order, its detail the sorted details of all the sites it replaces, so neither the specialization order nor a second variable on the line changes what the log says.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.one_per_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.overspecialized_anonymous_functions-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Anonymous functions of mod that capture a type or function, so each value compiles a new instance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.overspecialized_anonymous_functions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.package_type-Tuple{Symbol, Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether type name head resolves in scope to a type that neither Base nor Core defines.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.package_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.place_site-Tuple{AbstractVector{Site}, Tuple{String, String, Int64, Int64}}","page":"Source rules","text":"The one site of sites at place (key, file and lines), its detail theirs sorted and joined.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.place_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.plain_capture-Tuple{Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether a capture of type type is plain immutable data: a non-function isbits value, a String or Symbol, or an immutable struct, tuple or small Union of such. Arrays, Refs, mutable structs, types, functions, modules and Core.Box are not.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.plain_capture"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.present_directories-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Source rules","text":"The directories that exist in repository (a job's copy holds only src, ext, test and links).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.present_directories"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.range_guards-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{Corset.Located}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Overflow and underflow guards, keyed by the function they sit in.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.range_guards"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.reached-Tuple{Method, AbstractSet{Core.TypeName}, AbstractSet{Core.TypeName}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether current code reaches method: it is no closure's (closure_names), or its closure is live.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.reached"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.ref_sites-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"The Ref and RefValue names (REF_NAMES) of the Julia file path outside a C call, by name_sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ref_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.repeated_prefix-Tuple{DataType}","page":"Source rules","text":"repeated_prefix(type)\n\nThe word that the field names of type repeat instead of saying it once in the type: the type's own first word starting any field (SolverControls.solver_tolerance), or one first word shared by more than half of at least three fields (continuation_step, continuation_theta, ...: those fields belong in a ContinuationControls). nothing when no word repeats.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.repeated_prefix"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.repeated_statements-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{Corset.Located}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Statements that repeat an earlier statement of the same block, keyed definition: statement. A statement pasted twice runs twice; the same line in two branches is in two blocks and passes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.repeated_statements"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.resizes-Tuple{Expr, Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether parsed node resizes the variable name: a call of push!, empty! or another size-changing function on it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.resizes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.return_annotation-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"The declared return type of parsed function definition node, or nothing when it declares none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.return_annotation"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.return_type_calls-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{Corset.Located}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Calls of Core.Compiler.return_type, a guess at a result type, keyed by file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.return_type_calls"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.returns_argument_call-Tuple{Method}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether a return in method's lowered code returns a call to one of its arguments (f() in wrap(f) = f()): its result is that argument's, so the types its callers passed decide nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.returns_argument_call"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.returns_call-Tuple{Core.CodeInfo, AbstractUnitRange, Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether lowered statement of code returns a call to one of the arguments (slot numbers).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.returns_call"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.returns_concrete-Tuple{Corset.Located, Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether the definition item declares a return type naming a concrete type of scope, and is no constructor of its own type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.returns_concrete"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.signature_call-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"The call a parsed function definition node declares, whatever return annotation or where clause wraps it, or nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.signature_call"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.slot_line-Tuple{Core.CodeInfo, Method, Integer}","page":"Source rules","text":"The first statement of method's code that assigns slot index: where the variable is introduced, placed on its source line (the method's own line when no statement assigns it).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.slot_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.source_tree-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Source rules","text":"The syntax tree of the Julia file path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.source_tree"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.statement_hidden_inputs-Tuple{Core.CodeInfo, Method, Pair}","page":"Source rules","text":"The hidden_inputs sites of the lowered statement entry (index => statement) of method's code.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.statement_hidden_inputs"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.statement_line-Tuple{Union{Compiler.IRCode, Core.CodeInfo}, Method, Integer}","page":"Source rules","text":"statement_line(code, method, index)\n\nThe line of method's source that lowered statement index of code comes from: the line of the method itself for a statement from another file (a macro's).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.statement_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.struct_lines-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Source rules","text":"The struct syntax nodes at or below node, as name => line of the struct keyword (never the docstring's line above it).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.struct_lines"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.struct_locations-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Where each struct of the parsed source files is declared: its name with the file and line of its struct keyword, so a # lint: comment on that line opts the struct out even when a docstring sits above it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.struct_locations"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.struct_name-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Source rules","text":"The name a struct syntax node declares, whatever its parameters and supertype, as Julia names the type (var\"Odd Name\" gives Symbol(\"Odd Name\")).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.struct_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.struct_site-Tuple{Symbol, Dict{Symbol, Tuple{String, Int64}}}","page":"Source rules","text":"A Site keyed name at the declaration of struct name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.struct_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.testset_name-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"The name of the @testset that parsed expression node opens, or nothing when node opens none or the name is interpolated.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.testset_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.type_head-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"The type name at the head of parsed type expression annotation (Foo of Foo{T}), or nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.type_head"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.typed_frame-Tuple{Compiler.NativeInterpreter, Core.MethodMatch}","page":"Source rules","text":"The Inferred of method match match, or nothing when inference cannot type it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.typed_frame"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.typed_frames-Tuple{Type}","page":"Source rules","text":"typed_frames(signature)\n\nThe Inferred of every method signature selects. Each is inferred once: the unoptimized code is kept and the optimizer runs on a copy. A method inference cannot type (a generated method) is left out.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.typed_frames"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.unmarked_effects-Tuple{Repository, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Source rules","text":"Each method of is_unmarked_effect whose function has no method that returns a value, one site at its signature however many specializations ran: a function with a nothing method beside real ones (a dispatch on \"off\") is not a procedure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unmarked_effects"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.unstable_anonymous_functions-Tuple{Module}","page":"Source rules","text":"Anonymous functions of mod built where inference could not pin down the types of their captures.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unstable_anonymous_functions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.untyped_argument-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether a parsed argument of a method signature has no :: annotation (a bare name, alone or with a default or ...).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.untyped_argument"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.where_variables-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"The type variables parsed function definition node binds in its where clauses (T of T <: Real included).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.where_variables"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.without_lines-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Source rules","text":"Parsed source node with its line numbers dropped, so two copies of one statement compare equal.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.without_lines"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/source/#Corset.RULES","page":"Source rules","text":"Every rule, ordered by name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.RULES"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/source/#Corset.Context","page":"Source rules","text":"Everything a rule reads: the repository, the source directories that exist, the loaded package, its inferred frames, and the CandidateSearch the typed rules share.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Context"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.Context-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}, Union{Nothing, Module}}","page":"Source rules","text":"A Context with no inferred frames, for the rules that read no types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Context"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/source/#Corset.Rule","page":"Source rules","text":"A check with a name, a group (:default or :pedantic) and a one-line summary. The subtypes say what it reads: ModuleRule the loaded package, TreeRule the source directories as a whole, FileRule one parsed file at a time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Rule"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/source/#Corset.check","page":"Source rules","text":"check(rule, context)\ncheck(rule, context, path, located)\n\nThe Sites rule finds: in the whole context for a ModuleRule or TreeRule, in the file path (parsed as located) for a FileRule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.check"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.declared-Tuple{Corset.Context}","page":"Source rules","text":"Every struct the package defines with the file and line it is declared at, for placing a struct rule's sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.declared"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/source/#Corset.fix!","page":"Source rules","text":"Rewrite the source files so rule finds nothing. Only a fixable rule has a method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fix!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.fixable-Tuple{Corset.Rule}","page":"Source rules","text":"Whether rule has a fix!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fixable"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/source/#Corset.rule_group","page":"Source rules","text":":default for a rule that finds likely defects, :pedantic for one that enforces a style.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.rule_group"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/source/#Corset.rule_name","page":"Source rules","text":"The name of rule in baselines, opt-out comments and configuration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.rule_name"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/source/#Corset.rule_summary","page":"Source rules","text":"One line saying what rule finds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.rule_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.scope-Tuple{Corset.Context}","page":"Source rules","text":"The scope a FileRule resolves type names in: the loaded package, or Base when none is loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.scope"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/source/#Corset.struct_sites-Tuple{AbstractVector{DataType}, Corset.Context}","page":"Source rules","text":"The sites of the struct types, each placed at its declaration in context's sources.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.struct_sites"},{"category":"macro","location":"internals/source/#Corset.@rule-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Source rules","text":"@rule Kind \"name\" :group \"summary\" (context, path, located) -> body\n\nDefine the rule name (a ModuleRule, TreeRule or FileRule) whose check is body, with the parameters of its kind bound as written: context for the first two, context, path and located for a FileRule. The type is the rule name in CamelCase with Rule appended.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.@rule"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/typed/#Typed-code-rules","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Rules that read inferred code: the entry walk, runtime-dispatch candidates, mutation, dispatch, float widening, JET, Float64 operations and non-public access.","title":"Typed-code rules"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/typed/#Entry-signatures","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Corset.Entries finds the concrete call signatures a walk starts from. It reads only a Module, paths and types.","title":"Entry signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.entry_frames-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Type}, Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"entry_frames(seeds, target)\n\nThe typed_frames of every signature reachable from seeds (entry-point call signatures such as Tuple{typeof(f), Int}) along frame_callees edges, the seeds included; empty where inference yields none. Pass them to inferred_methods, which then infers nothing again.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.entry_frames"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.followed-Tuple{Any, Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether a walk of target follows callee, an invoked_instance: a method of target, or one whose signature names a type of it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.followed"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.frame_callees-Tuple{Compiler.IRCode, Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"frame_callees(ir, target)\n\nThe signatures ir, an optimized method body, calls through :invoke edges and a walk of target follows: callees defined in target or whose signature names one of its types (JET's target_modules scope).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.frame_callees"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.invoked_instance-Tuple{Core.MethodInstance}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"invoked_instance(callee)\n\nThe method instance an :invoke statement names: a CodeInstance on Julia 1.12 and later.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.invoked_instance"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.mentions_module-Tuple{Any, Module, Integer}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"mentions_module(signature, target, depth)\n\nWhether signature names a type defined in target anywhere in its parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.mentions_module"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.new_callees-Tuple{AbstractDict{Type}, AbstractVector{<:Type}, Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The signatures the frontier frames call that frames does not hold yet.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.new_callees"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.signature_callees-Tuple{AbstractDict{Type}, Type, Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The signatures the frames of signature call (frame_callees).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.signature_callees"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.DEFAULT_CANDIDATE_LIMIT","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The candidate_limit a search uses unless told otherwise: the most methods one runtime-dispatch site lists.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.DEFAULT_CANDIDATE_LIMIT"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.CandidateSearch","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"A candidate search: at most limit methods per runtime-dispatch call (0 lists none), and every frame inferred so far by method instance, nothing where inference failed. Searches that share frames infer no frame twice.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.CandidateSearch"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.CandidateSearch-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"CandidateSearch(inferred; candidate_limit = DEFAULT_CANDIDATE_LIMIT)\n\nA search seeded with the rules' own inferred frames. A negative candidate_limit throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.CandidateSearch"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Candidates","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The methods a runtime-dispatch call may reach, each inferred over its intersection with the call's signature. complete is false when the budget ran out, the call has no plain signature (a splat, a Core.invoke), or inference failed on a candidate; frames then holds the candidates it did type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Candidates"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.call_candidates-Tuple{Expr, Compiler.IRCode, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"call_candidates(statement, ir, search)\n\nThe Candidates of the runtime-dispatch statement of ir: none and incomplete past search.limit methods.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.call_candidates"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.call_signature-Tuple{Expr, Compiler.IRCode}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The abstract signature of :call statement statement from its inferred operand types; nothing for a builtin's call.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.call_signature"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.candidate_frame-Tuple{Corset.CandidateSearch, Core.MethodMatch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The frame of method match match, inferred once per search's frames; nothing when inference cannot type it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.candidate_frame"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.candidate_name-Tuple{Method}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The name a site's detail gives candidate method: its module, name, file and line.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.candidate_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.with_limit-Tuple{Corset.CandidateSearch, Integer}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The same search, sharing search's frames, with the budget limit.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.with_limit"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.ArgumentWrites","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"What a frame or statement does to arguments, as indices: those it writes through, those it passes to a runtime dispatch it cannot resolve, and those it passes to a ccall. The analysis cannot read the last two callees. writers pairs a written index with the runtime-dispatch candidate that writes it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ArgumentWrites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.alias_indices-Tuple{Integer, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The indices escape analysis puts in one alias set with index, index included.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.alias_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.argument_writes-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, AbstractDict{Core.MethodInstance, Corset.Inferred}, Tuple, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"argument_writes(frame, frames, stack, search)\n\nThe ArgumentWrites of frame, as argument numbers; a written argument is neither dispatched nor foreign. A statically resolved callee writes the arguments its own frame in frames (keyed by method instance) writes; a callee named with ! writes its first argument; any other callee writes none. A runtime dispatch writes what its call_candidates in search write (dispatch_writes). stack holds the instances being summarized, which a recursive call skips.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.argument_writes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.called_builtin-Tuple{Expr, Compiler.IRCode}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The builtin or intrinsic a :call statement calls; nothing for a generic function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.called_builtin"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.candidate_argument-Tuple{Method, Integer}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The argument of method that call operand position binds: a varargs method gathers the trailing operands into its last.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.candidate_argument"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.candidate_writes-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, AbstractDict{Core.MethodInstance, Corset.Inferred}, Tuple, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The ArgumentWrites of candidate frame, summarized with frame pushed on stack.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.candidate_writes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.declared_io-Tuple{Method, Integer}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether method declares argument index as an abstract IO (io::IO, io::T where T <: IO): it writes whatever stream its caller passes, an OS handle included, so a specialization's IOBuffer does not count.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.declared_io"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.dispatch_writes-Tuple{Expr, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState, AbstractDict{Core.MethodInstance, Corset.Inferred}, Tuple, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The ArgumentWrites of runtime-dispatch statement, read from its call_candidates. An operand a candidate writes is written, and names that candidate. An operand stays dispatched (unresolved) when the candidates are incomplete, one is on stack, or one passes it on to a dispatch or a ccall.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.dispatch_writes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.effect_arguments-Tuple{Symbol, AbstractVector{Corset.ArgumentWrites}, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The arguments that the field operands of the statement effects reach (reached_arguments).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.effect_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.escape_state-Tuple{Compiler.IRCode, Integer}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The escape analysis of ir, a method body of nargs arguments, in the current world.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.escape_state"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.invoked_writes-Tuple{Expr, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState, AbstractDict{Core.MethodInstance, Corset.Inferred}, Tuple, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The indices of the operands of :invoke statement statement that its callee writes (argument_writes).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.invoked_writes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.mutation_sites-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, AbstractDict{Core.MethodInstance, Corset.Inferred}, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The unmarked_mutations sites of item, one per written or unverified argument.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.mutation_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.operand_index-Tuple{Union{Core.Argument, Core.SSAValue}, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The escape-analysis index of IR operand operand; nothing for a constant or a global.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.operand_index"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.operand_indices-Tuple{AbstractVector, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The indices of the IR operands operands that escape analysis tracks.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.operand_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.os_context-Tuple{DataType}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether type is an IOContext around an os_handle.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.os_context"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.os_handle-Tuple{Type}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether every value of type type is an OS-backed handle: an OS_HANDLES type or a libuv stream other than the in-memory BufferStream.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.os_handle"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.position_writers-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, Corset.ArgumentWrites, AbstractVector{Int64}, AbstractVector, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The operand indices at positions of call operands that candidate frame writes (effect), each paired with its method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.position_writers"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.reached_arguments-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The arguments (2 and up; 1 is the function itself) whose memory the values at indices may point into: their escape-analysis aliases, closed under the memory a MEMORY_VIEWS result views.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.reached_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.reached_writers-Tuple{Corset.ArgumentWrites, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The writers of statement effect, each index replaced by the arguments it reaches.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.reached_writers"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.statement_writes-Tuple{Any, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState, AbstractDict, Tuple, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The ArgumentWrites of one IR statement, as the indices of its operands.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.statement_writes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.unmarked_mutations-Tuple{Repository, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"unmarked_mutations(repository, inferred; search = CandidateSearch(inferred))\n\nEach is_unmarked_method among inferred whose frame writes through one of its arguments, one site per method: \"writes argument x\", or \"may write\" when the argument reaches a ccall or a runtime dispatch whose call_candidates in search are incomplete. runtime-dispatch reports the dispatch itself. A write by a runtime-dispatch candidate names the candidate. A writing method added to another module's function (Base.length, Base.iterate) breaks what its callers expect.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unmarked_mutations"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.unresolved_positions-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, Corset.ArgumentWrites, AbstractVector{Int64}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The positions whose argument candidate frame passes on to a dispatch or a ccall (effect).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unresolved_positions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.view_sources-Tuple{Integer, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The aliases of the memory that SSA index index views when its statement is a MEMORY_VIEWS call; none otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.view_sources"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.writable-Tuple{Type}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether a write through a value of type type changes a Julia object: not plain_capture data, a type or a module, and not an os_handle, whose writes reach the file system or the OS.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.writable"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.writable_operands-Tuple{AbstractVector, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The indices of the operands whose IR type is writable. A call cannot write a Symbol or a bits value (a Ptr too, which C reads by value) it is passed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.writable_operands"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.writable_positions-Tuple{AbstractVector, Compiler.IRCode}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The positions (2 and up) of operands, a call's arguments with its callee first, whose IR type is writable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.writable_positions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.writer_arguments-Tuple{Pair{Int64, Method}, Compiler.IRCode, Base.Compiler.EscapeAnalysis.EscapeState}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The arguments the index of writer reaches (reached_arguments), each paired with its candidate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.writer_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.writer_note-Tuple{Integer, AbstractVector{Pair{Int64, Method}}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The note naming the runtime-dispatch candidates that write argument, among writers; empty when none does.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.writer_note"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.written_detail-Tuple{AbstractString, Method}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The detail of a site where method writes its argument name, naming the owner of a function another module owns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.written_detail"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.audited_frames-Tuple{Repository, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}, AbstractString}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The inferred frames whose method is in repository's own files and whose first line carries no # lint: rule opt-out, which so covers the whole method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.audited_frames"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.compiled_concretely-Tuple{Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"compiled_concretely(return_type)\n\nWhether a caller compiles against return_type: concrete, Union{} (always throws), a Type{X} constant, a union of at most UNION_SPLIT_LIMIT concrete members, which Julia splits, or a fixed-length tuple whose members each compile concretely.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.compiled_concretely"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.dispatch_sites-Tuple{Corset.Inferred}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The runtime_dispatches sites of item, one per dispatching statement, placed at its line in the method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.dispatch_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.dispatches-Tuple{Expr, Compiler.IRCode}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether statement of ir dispatches at run time: a :call of a generic function, or of a builtin that calls one (CALLING_BUILTINS). A logging hand-off (logging_call) dispatches by design.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.dispatches"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.logging_argument-Tuple{Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether a call argument names Base.CoreLogging or its handle_message.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.logging_argument"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.logging_call-Tuple{Expr}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"logging_call(statement)\n\nWhether a :call statement is a logging macro's hand-off to the current logger, which is an AbstractLogger chosen at runtime and so always dispatches.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.logging_call"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.opted_out-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, AbstractDict{String, Corset.OptOuts}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether the first line of item's method is among the opted-out lines skipped holds for its file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.opted_out"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.runtime_dispatches-Tuple{Repository, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"runtime_dispatches(repository, inferred)\n\nEach call the compiler leaves to run-time dispatch (dispatches) in a frame of inferred that audited_frames keeps, one site per method and source line.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.runtime_dispatches"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.widened_returns-Tuple{Repository, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"widened_returns(repository, inferred)\n\nEach method of inferred (as audited_frames keeps them) whose inferred result does not compile concretely (compiled_concretely), one site at its first line however many specializations ran.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.widened_returns"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.FloatBudget","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"A frame's float budget: the floats its arguments hold, and the precision (bits) of the widest. A statement whose result holds a float of more precision widens.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.FloatBudget"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Operand","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"One IR operand as the rule reads it: whether the frame computed it (an argument or SSA value, which widens nothing itself), the floats it brings in, and how a detail names it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Operand"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Operand-Tuple{Any, Compiler.IRCode}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The Operand of IR value operand in ir. A type operand (Float64 in sitofp(Float64, n)) brings in its own float.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Operand"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.callee_label-Tuple{Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The callee an IR call statement names: an :invoke's method, else its first argument. Another statement is named by its type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.callee_label"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.carries_floats-Tuple{Type, Corset.FloatBudget}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether a value of type type may hold a float of budget: it may be one, or holds one in a parameter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.carries_floats"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.dispatch_widening-Tuple{Expr, Compiler.IRCode, Corset.FloatBudget, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The detail of runtime-dispatch statement of ir under budget: a candidate whose result holds a wider float makes it definite; an incomplete list makes it \"may widen\". A dispatch whose operand types hold none of the floats budget receives is skipped (nothing).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.dispatch_widening"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.float_budget-Tuple{Corset.Inferred}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The FloatBudget of item, from its argument types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.float_budget"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.float_widenings-Tuple{Repository, AbstractVector{Corset.Inferred}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"float_widenings(repository, inferred; search = CandidateSearch(inferred))\n\nEach statement of an audited frame (audited_frames) whose float result is wider than every float its method receives in its arguments (x::Float32 * 2.0, float(n) in a Float32 method), one site per method and line. A frame with no float argument, or one as wide as Float64, is skipped. A runtime dispatch is judged by its call_candidates in search (dispatch_widening).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.float_widenings"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.frame_widenings-Tuple{Corset.Inferred, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The float_widenings sites of item, one per widening statement.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.frame_widenings"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.held_floats-Tuple{Any, Integer}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The concrete float types type holds: itself, or any type parameter at depth below 5 (Vector{Float32}, Complex{Float64}, Tuple{Int, Float16}), each union member included.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.held_floats"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.ir_label-Tuple{Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"How a detail names IR value operand. Julia 1.14 keeps a global as a Core.BindingPartition, named by its binding.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ir_label"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.judged-Tuple{Corset.FloatBudget}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether a frame of budget is judged: it receives a float, and none as wide as Float64.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.judged"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.result_floats-Tuple{Any, Any, AbstractVector{Corset.Operand}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The floats IR statement statement makes: those of its inferred type, or a return's value's (its operands).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.result_floats"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.returned_operands-Tuple{Core.ReturnNode, Compiler.IRCode}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The Operand a return returns: none for an unreachable one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.returned_operands"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.statement_operands-Tuple{Expr, Compiler.IRCode}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The Operands of IR statement statement: an Expr's arguments past an :invoke's instance, a φ's values, a π's or a return's value, a global read itself.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.statement_operands"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.statement_widening-Tuple{Any, Any, Compiler.IRCode, Corset.FloatBudget, Corset.CandidateSearch}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The widening detail of IR statement statement of type type: a dispatch's (dispatch_widening) or another's (widening_detail).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.statement_widening"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.value_floats-Tuple{Type}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The floats a value of IR type type holds; a Type{Float64} value holds no float.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.value_floats"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.widening_detail-Tuple{Any, Any, Compiler.IRCode, Corset.FloatBudget}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The detail of IR statement statement, of inferred type type, when it widens: its result holds a float wider than budget and no computed operand already did. It names the first operand that brings the wide float in, else the callee; nothing when the statement does not widen.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.widening_detail"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.widening_source-Tuple{Any, AbstractVector{Corset.Operand}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"How a widening detail names its source: the first of the wide operands, else the callee of statement.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.widening_source"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.wider-Tuple{AbstractVector{DataType}, Corset.FloatBudget}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether floats hold one wider than budget allows.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.wider"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.widest-Tuple{AbstractVector{DataType}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The widest of floats, by precision; floats holds at least one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.widest"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.jet_assertion-Tuple{Symbol, String, LineNumberNode, Symbol, Tuple}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The code of @call_sites and @opt_sites: sites gains the sites of report_macro run on arguments.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.jet_assertion"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.jet_site-Tuple{String, Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The Site of JET report report: its innermost frame names the function and the line.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.jet_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.jet_sites-Tuple{String, Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"One site per report of JET analysis result.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.jet_sites"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.loaded_jet","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The JET module among modules (the caller's loaded modules); throws when none is, naming the fix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.loaded_jet"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.float64_line-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether LLVM IR line is a double operation in FLOAT64_IR_OPS.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.float64_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.access_key-Tuple{NamedTuple}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The name of a qualified access row and the module it reaches the name in.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.access_key"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.entry_file-Tuple{Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The file mod was loaded from: its package entry file, or else the one source file its methods name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.entry_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.is_qualified-Tuple{Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether the ExplicitImports per-use row use is a qualified access (Module.name).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_qualified"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.non_public_accesses","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"non_public_accesses(mod, file = entry_file(mod))\n\nEach name of another module that mod reaches by qualified access (Base.JuliaSyntax) or explicit import (using Base: uniontypes) though that module neither exports it nor declares it public. ExplicitImports reads file and the files it includes. A qualified access has a site per use; an explicit import has one per name, at its first import.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.non_public_accesses"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.non_public_site-Tuple{NamedTuple, Union{Module, Symbol}}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The site of the ExplicitImports finding row, a name of the module owner, keyed Owner.name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.non_public_site"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.qualified_uses-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Module, AbstractVector{T}, Any}} where T<:NamedTuple","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Every qualified use in submodule, from the ExplicitImports file analysis, of a non-public name that findings (ExplicitImports rows, one per name) report.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.qualified_uses"},{"category":"module","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Entry signatures of a loaded module: concrete call signatures such as Tuple{typeof(f), Int} that a type-inference walk can start from. Each source is one function of a Module and paths; entry_signatures takes the union of the sources it names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.SOURCES","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The sources source_signatures and entry_signatures accept.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.SOURCES"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.binding_methods-Tuple{Any, Type}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The methods of binding value when it is a kind: a function's methods, or a type's constructors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.binding_methods"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.call_methods-Tuple{Any, Integer}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The methods that call an instance of binding value when it is a struct type; none otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.call_methods"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.compiled_signatures-Tuple{Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"compiled_signatures(mod)\n\nThe concrete signatures the running process has specialized mod's methods on: those a package image's precompile workload compiled, and those compiled since loading.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.compiled_signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.configured_signatures-Tuple{AbstractString, Symbol}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"configured_signatures(path, name)\n\nThe signatures the function name of the file path returns. The file is included in a fresh module; the function takes no arguments and returns a vector of signature types. Any other result throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.configured_signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.declared_signatures-Tuple{Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"declared_signatures(mod)\n\nThe signatures of mod's methods whose declared argument types are all concrete already.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.declared_signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.defined_methods-Tuple{Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"defined_methods(mod)\n\nThe methods mod defines on its own functions and types, closures included: each function's methods, and each type's constructors and call methods.\n\nponytail: methods mod adds to another module's function (Base.show, AD rules) are missed; Base.visit over the method table finds those but misses closure call methods on Julia 1.13 and needs a mutating callback.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.defined_methods"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.defines-Tuple{Module, Any}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"Whether signature is a concrete call signature that selects a method mod defines.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.defines"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.entry_signatures-Tuple{Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"entry_signatures(mod; sources = (:compiled, :declared), root = nothing, output = devnull, unset = ())\n\nThe union of the source_signatures of mod from each of sources, each signature once.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.entry_signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.module_bindings-Tuple{Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The values bound to the names of mod, unexported and compiler-made names included.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.module_bindings"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.source_signatures-Tuple{Module, Symbol}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"source_signatures(mod, source; root = nothing, output = devnull, unset = ())\n\nThe entry signatures of mod from one of SOURCES: :compiled (compiled_signatures), :declared (declared_signatures) or :tests (the trace_signatures of the package at root's test_trace, its test output written to output, the variables unset removed from its environment).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.source_signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.test_trace-Tuple{AbstractString, IO}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"test_trace(root, output; unset = ())\n\nRun the tests of the package at root (Pkg.test) in a child process started with --trace-compile, writing its output to output, and return the trace file's path. The child inherits every environment variable except those named in unset. A failing test run throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.test_trace"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.trace_scope-Tuple{Module}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"A module that binds every loaded package by name, and mod, so a trace line's qualified type names resolve.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.trace_scope"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.trace_signatures-Tuple{Module, AbstractString}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"trace_signatures(mod, trace)\n\nThe signatures in the precompile(Tuple{...}) lines of the --trace-compile file trace that select a method mod defines. A line whose type does not evaluate in this process (a type the test files define) is dropped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.trace_signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/typed/#Corset.Entries.traced_type-Tuple{Module, AbstractString}","page":"Typed-code rules","text":"The type of the trace line line, precompile(Tuple{...}), evaluated in scope; nothing for any other line or one that fails to evaluate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Entries.traced_type"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Guide","page":"Guide","text":"","title":"Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#The-pieces","page":"Guide","text":"A rule is a function from code to a vector of Sites. A site has a key (the name of the offender, such as \"Demo.jl total\"), a file, a line and a detail (what the offender is, such as local xAny; \"\" when the key says it all). The log of a failing rule prints each key's details.\n\nA Repository is the tree the rules read, plus the settings that relax them.\n\nratchet!(repo, \"rule-name\", sites) holds the sites to the repository's allowances and runs one @test. The rule name is a label you choose. It names the rule's table in the baseline file and the rule in opt-out comments. offenders! does the same without the @test.\n\nThere are two kinds of rules.\n\nModule rules read a loaded module: hidden_inputs(MyPackage), impure_anonymous_functions(MyPackage), abstract_locals(repo, inferred_methods(MyPackage, SIGNATURES)).\nSource rules read a file's syntax. Parse each file once with located_source, then hand it to each rule: nothing_returns(file, located_source(file)). repository_sources(repo, (\"src\",)) lists a repository's files.\n\n@testset \"code rules\" begin\n    files = repository_sources(REPO, (\"src\",))\n    ratchet!(REPO, \"nothing-return\",\n        [site for file in files for site in nothing_returns(file, located_source(file))])\nend","title":"The pieces"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Adopting-Corset-on-an-existing-package","page":"Guide","text":"Turning on a rule in a mature package usually reports hundreds of offenders. A baseline makes that adoptable. It allows today's offenders, fails on new ones, and lowers itself as old ones are fixed.\n\nconst REPO = Repository(pkgdir(MyPackage); baseline = joinpath(@__DIR__, \"code_baseline.toml\"))\n\nCreate an empty code_baseline.toml and run the tests. A rule without a table is seeded with its current offenders and passes:\n\n[hidden-input]\n\"COUNTER\" = 1\n\n[abstract-local]\n\"Demo.jl total\" = 1\n\nEach entry is a key and an allowance. An integer allows that many sites under the key. A string, such as \"kept: hot loop\", is a note that allows any number.\n\nAfter that:\n\nA new offender fails the test, because its key has no entry or the entry's count is exceeded.\nA fixed offender lowers the file. When a run finds fewer sites than an entry allows, the entry falls to the new count, or is deleted at zero, and the file is rewritten. Commit the change. The allowance can only shrink.\n\nA testset that measures only part of a rule's keys passes the key prefixes it covers as scopes, so entries outside them never fall.\n\nratchet!(REPO, \"abstract-local\", sites; scopes = (\"Parser.jl\",))","title":"Adopting Corset on an existing package"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Telling-the-reader-how-to-repair-an-offender","page":"Guide","text":"fix adds a line to the failure log:\n\nratchet!(REPO, \"concrete-return\", sites; fix = Corset.CONCRETE_RETURN_FIX)","title":"Telling the reader how to repair an offender"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Exemptions","page":"Guide","text":"Two settings on the Repository relax rules for a whole project:\n\nRepository(root; one_letter_exempt = (:p,), skipped_directories = (\"vendor\",))\n\none_letter_exempt lists variable names the one-letter rule allows besides _. A project's own convention, such as an argument everywhere named p, goes here. skipped_directories lists directory names that repository_sources leaves out wherever they sit. Hidden directories are always left out.","title":"Exemptions"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Opting-out-one-site","page":"Guide","text":"A comment opts a site out of a rule by the rule's name:\n\nconst CACHE = Ref(0)   # lint: hidden-input  memoized across calls on purpose\n\nComment Opts out\n# lint: RULE its own line\n# lint: RULE-begin … # lint: RULE-end the lines between, inclusive\n# lint: RULE-file the whole file\n\nWrite the reason after the rule name. A -begin with no -end runs to the end of the file. ratchet! logs how many sites each rule's opt-outs removed.","title":"Opting out one site"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#JET","page":"Guide","text":"@call_sites and @opt_sites turn JET.@report_call and JET.@report_opt reports into sites. Each report becomes one site keyed by scope, function and report kind.\n\nsites = Site[]\n@call_sites \"parse\" sites target_modules = (MyPackage,) MyPackage.parse(\"1 + 2\")\nratchet!(REPO, \"jet\", sites)","title":"JET"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Float32-code-paths","page":"Guide","text":"A wrapper number type catches Float64 only when it is promoted with a wrapped number. A dependency that computes at Float64 internally and narrows before returning stays invisible to it. float64_ops reads the optimized IR of one call and counts Float64 operations:\n\n@test float64_ops(my_kernel, (Float32, Vector{Float32})) == 0\n\nKeep a positive control, a function that does use Float64, so a change to the IR filter cannot disarm the check.","title":"Float32 code paths"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/runner/#Runner","page":"Runner","text":"The ratchet, configuration, the check runner, the CLI, imports, undefined names and where returns.","title":"Runner"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.OPT_OUT","page":"Runner","text":"# lint: RULE opts its own line out of RULE, # lint: RULE-begin … # lint: RULE-end the lines between (inclusive), # lint: RULE-file the whole file; the reason follows on the comment. A rule name is lowercase words joined by -.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.OPT_OUT"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.Baseline","page":"Runner","text":"A baseline file: per rule, the allowance (a count or a note) of each offender.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Baseline"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.OptOuts","page":"Runner","text":"Which lines of one file a rule skips: all of them when whole_file, else lines.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.OptOuts"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.checked_line_limit-Tuple{Integer, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"limit, a file_line_limit set by source; one below 1 throws, since it would report every file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.checked_line_limit"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.detail_lines-Union{Tuple{AbstractVector{S}}, Tuple{S}} where S<:Site","page":"Runner","text":"The details of the sites under each key, sorted and joined; a key none of whose sites has one is absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.detail_lines"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.detail_suffix-Tuple{AbstractDict{String, String}, String}","page":"Runner","text":"The parenthesized detail that follows key in the log, empty when key has none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.detail_suffix"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.entered_directory-Tuple{AbstractString, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether julia_files enters entry: a directory, not a link, not hidden and not named in skipped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.entered_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.exceeded-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractDict{String, Int64}, String}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether baseline table entries does not allow the measured count of key: absent, or past its count.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.exceeded"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.exceeding-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractDict{String, Int64}}","page":"Runner","text":"The keys of measured that baseline table entries does not allow: absent from it, or past their count.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.exceeding"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.exceeds-Tuple{Integer, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether found sites exceed baseline entry; a note allows any number.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.exceeds"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.falling-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractDict{String, Int64}, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"The keys of entries under one of scopes that measured undercuts, so their entry can be lowered.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.falling"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.falls-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractDict{String, Int64}, Tuple{Vararg{String}}, String}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether key of entries is under one of scopes and measured undercuts its entry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.falls"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.julia_file-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether entry is a Julia file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.julia_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.julia_files-Tuple{AbstractString, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"The Julia files below directory, in no particular order; hidden directories, those named in skipped and links to directories are not entered.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.julia_files"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.key_details-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Site}, String}","page":"Runner","text":"The details of the sites under key, sorted and joined.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.key_details"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.logged_over-Tuple{String, AbstractDict{String, Int64}, AbstractDict{String, String}, AbstractVector{String}, String, String}","page":"Runner","text":"Log over, the keys of measured past what allowance names allows, each with its details, and with fix (how to repair one) when given; return over.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.logged_over"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.opt_outs-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"opt_outs(path, rule)\n\nThe lines of path that the # lint: comments (OPT_OUT) take out of rule. A -begin without an -end runs to the end of the file. A path that is no file (a method a macro defined has the file none) has none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.opt_outs"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.over_line-Tuple{AbstractDict{String, Int64}, AbstractDict{String, String}, String}","page":"Runner","text":"The log line of offender key: its count in measured and its details.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.over_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.read_baseline-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The baseline in the TOML file at path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.read_baseline"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.remaining-Tuple{AbstractString, Integer}","page":"Runner","text":"The baseline entry left after found sites against entry: a note stays while its offender has a site, a count falls to found.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.remaining"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.repository_sources-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"The Julia files under directories of repository; hidden directories and its skipped_directories are left out.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.repository_sources"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.tally-Union{Tuple{AbstractVector{S}}, Tuple{S}} where S<:Site","page":"Runner","text":"The number of sites under each key.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.tally"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.unopted-Union{Tuple{S}, Tuple{AbstractVector{S}, AbstractString}} where S<:Site","page":"Runner","text":"The sites of sites that no # lint: comment naming rule opts out, and how many were opted out.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unopted"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.write_baseline!-Tuple{Dict{String, Dict{String, Union{Int64, String}}}, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"Write baseline to the file at path in one rename, so a reader never sees half a file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.write_baseline!"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.Config","page":"Runner","text":"Config\n\nWhat a project sets for corset: the source directories to read, the baseline file, the Repository exemptions, whether the pedantic group is on, and per-rule levels (:allow, :warn or :deny) that override a rule's group, the candidate_limit of the typed rules' CandidateSearch, the file_line_limit of the file-length rule, and the entry_points (file => function, the file relative to the project) whose signatures replace the --entries sources.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Config"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.Preferences","page":"Runner","text":"One [Corset] preferences table, as written: a key left out is nothing, so a layer overlays another key by key.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Preferences"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.checked_limit-Tuple{Integer, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"limit, a candidate_limit set by source; a negative one throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.checked_limit"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.entry_point-Tuple{Nothing}","page":"Runner","text":"The file => function of an entry_points setting \"file.jl:function\"; nothing when unset. Any other shape throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.entry_point"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.level-Tuple{Corset.Config, Corset.Rule}","page":"Runner","text":"The level config gives rule: its own setting, else :warn for the default group and for the pedantic group when on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.level"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.load_config-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"load_config(root)\n\nThe Config of the project at root: the [preferences.Corset] table of its Project.toml overlaid by the [Corset] table of its LocalPreferences.toml, key by key. An unknown key, an unknown rule name or a level other than allow, warn or deny throws, so a typo cannot silently switch a rule off.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.load_config"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.merged-Tuple{Dict, Dict}","page":"Runner","text":"Merge two preference dictionaries, with over overriding matching keys in under.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.merged"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.overlay-Tuple{Corset.Preferences, Corset.Preferences}","page":"Runner","text":"over's keys where it sets them, else under's; nested dictionaries are merged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.overlay"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.read_preferences-Tuple{AbstractString, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"The preferences in the TOML file below the path of table names ((\"preferences\", \"Corset\")); none set when there is no file or table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.read_preferences"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.repository-Tuple{Corset.Config, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The Repository for config rooted at root; a relative baseline path is taken from root.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.repository"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.Finding","page":"Runner","text":"One site a rule found, with the level it was found at.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.Finding"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.allowances-Tuple{Repository, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The allowances the baseline file of repository holds for rule: none when there is no file or no table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.allowances"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.apply_fix!-Tuple{Corset.Rule, Corset.Context}","page":"Runner","text":"Run the fixer of rule over the files context names, when rule has one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.apply_fix!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.apply_fixes!-Tuple{Tuple{}, Corset.Context}","page":"Runner","text":"Run the fixer of every fixable rule in rules over the files context names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.apply_fixes!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.can_run-Tuple{Corset.Rule, Union{Nothing, Module}, Union{Nothing, AbstractDict{Type, Vector{Corset.Inferred}}, AbstractVector{<:Type}}}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether rule has what it reads: the loaded package mod for a module rule, signatures for a rule that reads inferred types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.can_run"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.disallowed_keys-Tuple{Repository, AbstractString, AbstractVector{Site}, AbstractVector{Site}, Bool}","page":"Runner","text":"The keys of kept sites that the baseline of repository does not allow for rule; with update, it is seeded and lowered as offenders! does.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.disallowed_keys"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.enabled_rules-Tuple{Corset.Config}","page":"Runner","text":"The rules config leaves on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.enabled_rules"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.file_diff-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The unified diff from the file before to the file after, labeled label; empty when they match.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.file_diff"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.fix_diff-Tuple{Corset.Config, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"fix_diff(config, root)\n\nThe unified diff of the rewrites --fix would make, computed on a copy of the source directories. The tree at root is not written.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fix_diff"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.is_on-Tuple{Corset.Config, Corset.Rule}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether config leaves rule on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_on"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.judge-Tuple{Repository, Corset.Rule, Symbol, AbstractVector{Site}, Bool}","page":"Runner","text":"The findings among sites of rule at level: the sites no # lint: comment opts out, whose key the baseline does not allow. With update, the baseline is seeded and lowered as offenders! does.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.judge"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.module_rule_names-Tuple{Tuple}","page":"Runner","text":"The names of the rules in rules that read the loaded package.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.module_rule_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.reads_signatures-Tuple{Corset.Rule}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether rule reads the types inference gives signatures (inferred_methods).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.reads_signatures"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.run_rules-Tuple{Corset.Config, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"run_rules(config, root; mod = nothing, signatures = nothing, fix = false, update_baseline = false)\n\nThe findings of every rule config leaves on, over the project at root, and the names of the rules skipped because they read the loaded package mod and none was given. The rules that read inferred types also need signatures: the fixed workload inferred_methods types mod over, or the frames entry_frames already inferred; without them they are skipped. fix first rewrites the files for the rules that have a fixer. update_baseline seeds and lowers the baseline file; without it the baseline is only read.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.run_rules"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.ENTRY_SOURCES","page":"Runner","text":"The Entries sources each --entries name stands for.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ENTRY_SOURCES"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.CheckOptions","page":"Runner","text":"The options of corset check, as ArgParse parsed them; overrides are the rule => level pairs of --allow, --warn and --deny.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.CheckOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.RulesOptions","page":"Runner","text":"The options of corset rules.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.RulesOptions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.argument_settings-Tuple{}","page":"Runner","text":"The command's argument table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.argument_settings"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.broken_pipe-Tuple{Any}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether error_ is a write to a closed pipe (corset rules | head), which ends the run quietly.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.broken_pipe"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.command_options-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"Runner","text":"The typed options of the command ArgParse parsed into parsed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.command_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.detail_note-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The (detail) a concise finding line ends with; empty for a site with no detail.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.detail_note"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.display_path-Tuple{AbstractString, Site}","page":"Runner","text":"The path of site relative to root; empty for a site with no file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.display_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.entry_sources-Tuple{Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Runner","text":"The Entries sources the --entries list entries (workload,tests) names, workload when it is nothing. An unknown name, or none beside another, throws.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.entry_sources"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.error_message-Tuple{ErrorException}","page":"Runner","text":"The message corset prints for a usage or configuration error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.error_message"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.exit_code-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.Finding}, Bool}","page":"Runner","text":"The exit code for findings: 1 for any deny-level finding, or any finding when deny_warnings; else 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.exit_code"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.level_overrides-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The rule => level pairs the option name (allow, warn or deny) of arguments sets.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.level_overrides"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.load_package-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The package at root, loaded in the running process.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.load_package"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.main-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}","page":"Runner","text":"run_command on the process's standard streams, as they are when the command starts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.main"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.option!-Tuple{ArgParse.ArgParseSettings, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"Add the argument or option name to settings with the ArgParse options (help, action, default, ...).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.option!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.print_findings-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{IO, AbstractString, AbstractVector{F}, AbstractString}} where F<:Corset.Finding","page":"Runner","text":"Print findings to io in format (human, concise or json).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.print_findings"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.print_fix_diff-Tuple{IO, Corset.Config, AbstractString, Bool}","page":"Runner","text":"corset check --diff: print the changes --fix would make to io; the exit code is 1 when there are any.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.print_fix_diff"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.print_rules-Tuple{IO, Corset.Config}","page":"Runner","text":"corset rules: one line per rule with its group and the level config gives it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.print_rules"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.project_root-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The directory of the project that contains path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.project_root"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.reads_package-Tuple{Corset.Config}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether any rule config leaves on reads the loaded package.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.reads_package"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.relaunch-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}","page":"Runner","text":"relaunch(root, args)\n\nReplace this process with a Julia process whose active project is root, running corset on args. Corset's own environment stays on the load path after the project's, so the project's versions of shared dependencies win. Where execv does not exist the command runs as a child and its exit code is returned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.relaunch"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.rethrow_arg_error-Tuple{ArgParse.ArgParseSettings, ArgParse.ArgParseError}","page":"Runner","text":"Rethrow an ArgParse error so run_command catches it and exits with 2.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.rethrow_arg_error"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.rule_line-Tuple{Corset.Config, Corset.Rule}","page":"Runner","text":"The corset rules line for rule: its name, group, the level config gives it, and its summary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.rule_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.run_command-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, IO, IO}","page":"Runner","text":"run_command(args, out, err)\n\nThe corset command on the streams out and err. Returns the exit code: 0 when clean, 1 when a finding fails the run, 2 on a usage or configuration error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.run_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.run_options-Tuple{Corset.CheckOptions, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, IO, IO}","page":"Runner","text":"Run corset check with options (from the command line args); returns the exit code.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.run_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.run_options-Tuple{Corset.RulesOptions, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, IO, IO}","page":"Runner","text":"Run corset rules: print the rules and their levels to out.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.run_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.seed_sources-Tuple{Corset.Config, AbstractString, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}, Module, IO}","page":"Runner","text":"The entry signatures of the loaded package mod at root, by source name: the entry_points of config alone when it sets them, else the entries sources. Test output goes to output; the tests run without this command's own environment variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.seed_sources"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.seed_summary-Tuple{AbstractVector{Pair{String, Vector{Type}}}, AbstractDict{Type}}","page":"Runner","text":"The line that says how many signatures each of sources gave, how many seeds their union holds, and how many signatures the walk frames inferred.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.seed_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.seeded_frames-Tuple{AbstractVector{Pair{String, Vector{Type}}}, Module, IO}","page":"Runner","text":"The entry_frames of mod the typed rules read, walked once from the union of sources, with seed_summary printed to output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.seeded_frames"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.with_overrides-Tuple{Corset.Config, Bool, AbstractVector{<:Pair{String, Symbol}}, Union{Nothing, Integer}}","page":"Runner","text":"config with the pedantic group switched on when pedantic is set, the levels in overrides (rule => level) applied, and candidate_limit set unless it is nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.with_overrides"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.ImportFile","page":"Runner","text":"A parsed Julia file: the names it uses outside imports, its import statements, and the paths it includes (\"\" for an include no literal names). An editable file is one the rule checks.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ImportFile"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.ImportItem","page":"Runner","text":"One name an import binds: name as code spells it (@test, s for r as s) and the text declaring it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ImportItem"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.ImportMove","page":"Runner","text":"An import item of statement that file does not use: it goes from file and is added to each of targets (none when no other file needs it).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ImportMove"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.ImportStatement","page":"Runner","text":"An import statement: prefix (using M: or import) before its items, at bytes first_byte:last_byte, starting on line. A pinned one (a bare using M, or opted out) stays. A nested one sits in a module block of its file and serves only that block and its includes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.ImportStatement"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.addition_edit-Tuple{Corset.ImportFile, AbstractVector{Pair{String, String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"The edit adding items (prefix => item text) to file: after its last import, at that import's indent, or at the top of a file with none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.addition_edit"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.expression_names-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Runner","text":"The names a parsed expression uses; a QuoteNode (a field name) uses none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.expression_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.file_moves-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportFile}, Bool, Corset.ImportFile}","page":"Runner","text":"The moves of the unpinned statements of file, one of unit; supplied when a bare using is in the unit.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.file_moves"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.has_bare_using-Tuple{Corset.ImportFile}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether file has a bare using M, which may bring in any name M exports.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.has_bare_using"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.import_file-Tuple{AbstractString, Bool}","page":"Runner","text":"Julia file path parsed for import placement; editable marks a file the rule checks and rewrites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.import_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.import_files-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"The Julia files of directories in repository, parsed for import placement.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.import_files"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.import_moves-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportFile}}","page":"Runner","text":"Every import move in files (the rule's own), module by module; a file in two modules is left alone.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.import_moves"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.import_nodes-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"Every using and import statement below node, outside quotes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.import_nodes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.import_sites-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportMove}}","page":"Runner","text":"One site per move, keyed by file and name, at the import's line.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.import_sites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.import_statement-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode, AbstractString, AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, Bool}","page":"Runner","text":"The statement a using or import node of text (split into lines) declares; nested when it sits in a module block.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.import_statement"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.imports_name-Tuple{Corset.ImportFile, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether file imports name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.imports_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.include_paths-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The paths the include calls below node name, relative to directory; \"\" for one whose path is not a literal.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.include_paths"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.inside_module-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode, AbstractVector{<:UnitRange}}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether node starts inside one of the byte ranges modules.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.inside_module"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.interpolated_names-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The names used by the interpolations in command text text, found by Julia's own Base.shell_parse (none inside single quotes).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.interpolated_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.is_blank-Tuple{Unsigned}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether byte is a space or tab.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_blank"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.is_literal_string-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether node is a string literal with no interpolation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_literal_string"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.item_name-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"The name parsed import item node binds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.item_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.line_end-Tuple{AbstractVector{UInt8}, Integer}","page":"Runner","text":"The last byte (the newline) of the line holding byte index of bytes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.line_end"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.line_start-Tuple{AbstractVector{UInt8}, Integer}","page":"Runner","text":"The first byte of the line holding byte index of bytes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.line_start"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.literal_pieces-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"The path pieces of include argument node: \"a.jl\" or joinpath(@__DIR__, \"a\", \"b.jl\"); empty for anything else.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.literal_pieces"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.misplaced_imports-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"misplaced_imports(repository, directories)\n\nOne site per import item in directories that its file does not use: one that no file of its module uses, or that other files of the module use. place_imports! fixes them.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.misplaced_imports"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.module_nodes-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"Every module block below node.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.module_nodes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.move_target-Tuple{Corset.ImportFile, Bool, Corset.ImportFile, Corset.ImportStatement, Corset.ImportItem}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether item of statement in file can move to other: it uses the name, does not import it, and a nested statement only moves into an include.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.move_target"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.move_targets-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportFile}, Bool, Corset.ImportFile, Corset.ImportStatement, Corset.ImportItem}","page":"Runner","text":"The files of unit that use item of statement in file without importing it, where the item can move.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.move_targets"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.moved_items-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportMove}, Corset.ImportStatement}","page":"Runner","text":"The items moves take out of statement.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.moved_items"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.name_tokens-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"The names syntax node uses: identifiers, macros and string macros, without field names and import statements.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.name_tokens"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.place_imports!-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"place_imports!(repository, directories)\n\nRewrite the Julia files of directories so every import sits in the files that use it: each misplaced_imports site is deleted, or moved into the module's files that use it. Returns the sites.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.place_imports!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.placeable-Tuple{Corset.ImportFile, Corset.ImportItem}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether item is a name the rule places and file does not use.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.placeable"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.placed_text-Tuple{Corset.ImportFile, AbstractVector{Corset.ImportMove}}","page":"Runner","text":"The text of file after moves: its moved items taken out, and the items moved to it added.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.placed_text"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.prefix_statement-Tuple{AbstractVector{Pair{String, String}}, String}","page":"Runner","text":"The import statement of the items (prefix => item text) under prefix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.prefix_statement"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.removal_edit-Tuple{AbstractVector{UInt8}, Corset.ImportStatement, AbstractVector{Corset.ImportItem}}","page":"Runner","text":"The edit taking removed items out of statement in bytes: the statement rewritten, or its whole lines deleted when nothing stays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.removal_edit"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.single_unit-Tuple{AbstractDict{String, Int64}, Corset.ImportMove}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether move's file and targets each sit in one unit of membership.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.single_unit"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.splice_text-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, UnitRange{Int64}, AbstractString}} where T<:AbstractString","page":"Runner","text":"The text text with the bytes of range replaced by replacement.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.splice_text"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.statement_imports-Tuple{Corset.ImportStatement, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether statement imports name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.statement_imports"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.statement_moves-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportFile}, Bool, Corset.ImportFile, Corset.ImportStatement}","page":"Runner","text":"The moves of the items of statement in file that file does not use.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.statement_moves"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.unit_count-Tuple{AbstractVector, String}","page":"Runner","text":"How many of units (each a module's files, ragged) hold the file at path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unit_count"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.unit_files-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractDict{String, Corset.ImportFile}, AbstractVector{String}}","page":"Runner","text":"The files of the module rooted at path: it and every file it includes, transitively. An include outside known is parsed as a file the rule reads but never rewrites; an unreadable one is a blank mark.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unit_files"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.unit_holds-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportFile}, String}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether unit holds the file at path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unit_holds"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.unit_moves-Tuple{AbstractVector{Corset.ImportFile}}","page":"Runner","text":"The moves in one module's unit; none when it holds an include the rule cannot follow. A bare using M anywhere in the unit may supply any name, so a file that uses a name without importing it is no target then. Files outside the checked directories (a vendored package's tests) bring their own imports, so they count as no user.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.unit_moves"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.assigned_names!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Runner","text":"Add every name an assignment to target binds: x, x::T, and tuples of those, nested.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.assigned_names!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.bound_names!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Runner","text":"bound_names!(names, node)\n\nAdd every name node binds anywhere to names: definitions, assignments, destructuring and imports.\n\nOver-approximated on purpose, so a reported name is one that nothing in reach defines.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.bound_names!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.declared_name-Tuple{Any}","page":"Runner","text":"The name a struct, abstract type or module declares, through <: and type parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.declared_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.enum_names!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Runner","text":"Add the names the arguments of a macro the scan does not know could bind, so a name only such a macro defines (@enum, @kwdef, @eval) is never reported: every bare symbol, x::T and x = v target among arguments, alone or in a begin block.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.enum_names!"},{"category":"function","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.follow_includes!","page":"Runner","text":"Add the names every file node includes by literal path binds to names, those files' includes too (visited stops cycles).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.follow_includes!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.import_names!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Runner","text":"import_names!(names, node)\n\nAdd the names a using or import statement binds to names.\n\nusing Mod: a, b binds a and b; using Mod binds whatever Mod exports, so the module is loaded to ask it; import Mod binds Mod alone.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.import_names!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.included_path-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"included_path(argument, directory)\n\nResolve an include argument to a path, or nothing when it is not a literal.\n\nOnly a string, @__DIR__ and joinpath of those resolve; any other expression is never evaluated, because scanning a file must not run its code.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.included_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.is_testset_macro-Tuple{Any}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether name is @testset or a qualified spelling of it such as Test.@testset.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_testset_macro"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.macro_name-Tuple{Any}","page":"Runner","text":"The macro a macrocall's head name calls, unqualified (Test.@testset gives @testset); Symbol(\"\") for any other head.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.macro_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.module_globals!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Runner","text":"module_globals!(names, value, scope)\n\nAdd every name lowered code resolves against scope to names.\n\nLowering resolves every local, so a name still reaching the module is either a real global or nothing at all.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.module_globals!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.path_pieces-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The strings argument joins (nothing when any part is not a literal).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.path_pieces"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.reads_only-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether macro name only reads its arguments (a test, logging or timing macro), so a bare symbol among them binds nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.reads_only"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.testset_nodes-Tuple{Any, Integer}","page":"Runner","text":"The (line, node) of every @testset under node, wherever a block, let or wrapper macro puts it; a testset's own body is not searched.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.testset_nodes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.without_imports-Tuple{Any}","page":"Runner","text":"without_imports(node)\n\nReturn node with every using and import statement dropped.\n\nusing is a top-level form, so a body carrying one cannot sit in a let. The names it binds are already in the defined set, so dropping it costs nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.without_imports"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.binds_an_argument-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether a variable the where clause of signature introduces occurs in the arguments of its call.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.binds_an_argument"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.fix_where_returns!-Tuple{Repository, Tuple{Vararg{String}}}","page":"Runner","text":"fix_where_returns!(repository, directories)\n\nRewrite the Julia files of directories with fix_where_returns. Returns the sites it fixed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fix_where_returns!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.fix_where_returns-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"fix_where_returns(text)\n\ntext with every short-form f(x)::R where {E} = … that uses E in its arguments written (f(x)::R) where {E} = …, the reading the long form function f(x)::R where {E} already has.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.fix_where_returns"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.identifier_names-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"The text of every identifier leaf under syntax node.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.identifier_names"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.is_where_return-Tuple{Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"Whether syntax node is a short-form method definition call::(R where …) = body.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.is_where_return"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.where_return_insertions!-Tuple{AbstractVector{Pair{Int64, String}}, Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"The byte insertions (position => text) that parenthesize the signatures under node as (call::R) where {…}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.where_return_insertions!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.where_return_sites!-Tuple{AbstractVector{Site}, AbstractString, Base.JuliaSyntax.SyntaxNode}","page":"Runner","text":"where_return_sites!(sites, path, node)\n\nPush a Site for each short-form definition under node whose where binds the return annotation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.where_return_sites!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/runner/#Corset.where_return_sites-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Runner","text":"The short-form definitions of the Julia file path whose where binds the return annotation, keyed by file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Corset.where_return_sites"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Rules","page":"Rules","text":"A rule name is the label you pass to ratchet! and write in opt-out comments. The names below are conventions; any lowercase words joined by - work.\n\nRules that need the compiler's answer read a loaded module. Rules about how code is written read source files.","title":"Rules"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Rules-on-a-loaded-module","page":"Rules","text":"These see inferred types, bindings and closures. They need using MyPackage. The rules that read inferred types take their signatures from the caller: inferred_methods(MyPackage, signatures) infers the methods those signatures reach, so the result is the same on every run. inferred_methods(MyPackage, entry_frames(seeds, MyPackage)) reads the frames an entry-point walk already inferred. The corset command line seeds that walk from Corset.Entries (see --entries in the CLI page). An opt-out on a method's first line covers every site these rules find in that method.","title":"Rules on a loaded module"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#hidden-input:-hidden_inputs(mod)","page":"Rules","text":"Reads of a non-constant or mutable global, or of a ScopedValue. The result of such a function depends on state its signature does not show.\n\nRepair: pass the value as an argument, or return it from the function that computes it.","title":"hidden-input: hidden_inputs(mod)"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#non-public-access:-non_public_accesses(mod)","page":"Rules","text":"Pedantic. Qualified accesses (Base.JuliaSyntax) and explicit imports (using Base: uniontypes) of a name its module neither exports nor declares public. Such a name can change in any release. ExplicitImports.jl finds them. A qualified access has a site per use, so an opt-out covers only its line.\n\nRepair: use a public name, or opt the line out with the reason the internal is needed.","title":"non-public-access: non_public_accesses(mod)"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#abstract-local:-abstract_locals(repo,-inferred_methods(mod,-signatures))","page":"Rules","text":"Local variables whose inferred type is abstract or a union, one site per variable however many specializations ran. The usual causes are an accumulator that starts as 0 and receives floats, and a variable assigned from a container of abstract type.\n\nRepair: initialize with the right type (zero(eltype(xs))) or annotate the local.","title":"abstract-local: abstract_locals(repo, inferred_methods(mod, signatures))"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#bang:-unmarked_effects(repo,-inferred_methods(mod,-signatures))","page":"Rules","text":"Functions that always return nothing and have no ! in the name. A function with a nothing method beside methods that return values (a dispatch on \"off\") is not reported.\n\nRepair: add the !.","title":"bang: unmarked_effects(repo, inferred_methods(mod, signatures))"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#unmarked-mutation:-unmarked_mutations(repo,-inferred_methods(mod,-signatures))","page":"Rules","text":"Functions without ! in the name that write through an argument: v[1] = 0, x.field = 1, push!(x.items, 1), or a write through an alias, a field or an element of the argument. The rule reads each frame's optimized IR and asks the compiler's escape analysis which arguments the written object aliases. A callee that is not inlined writes its first argument when its name ends in !, and what its own frame writes otherwise. At a runtime dispatch the rule lists the candidate methods (candidate_limit, default 4, in the [preferences.Corset] table, --candidate-limit on the command line, or unmarked_mutations(repo, inferred; search = CandidateSearch(inferred; candidate_limit))). When every candidate is listed and none writes the argument, the dispatch writes nothing. A candidate that writes it makes the write definite, and the detail names the candidate. An argument passed to a ccall, or to a dispatch with more candidates than the budget, a candidate inference cannot type, or a candidate that itself dispatches on the argument, is reported as one that may be written. runtime-dispatch reports the same dispatch. A method the package adds to another module's non-! function (Base.length, Base.iterate on a stateful iterator) is checked too: \"adds a writing method to Base.length, which callers expect not to write\". A write to any Julia object counts, an IOBuffer, a lock or a Channel included. Arguments that cannot be written in Julia are never reported: plain immutable data (bits values, Strings, Symbols), types, modules, and OS-backed handles (IOStream, files, pipes, sockets, terminals, processes), whose writes leave Julia. So is an IOContext around one. A method declaring an abstract IO argument (io::IO) writes whatever stream its caller passes, so it is not reported even when compiled for an IOBuffer; a concrete in-memory declaration (io::IOBuffer, io::IOContext{IOBuffer}) is. Escape analysis merges the alias sets of a value and the object it is stored in, so deepcopy_internal(x, stackdict), which stores x in stackdict, reports both.\n\nRepair: add the !, or copy the argument before writing to the copy.","title":"unmarked-mutation: unmarked_mutations(repo, inferred_methods(mod, signatures))"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#runtime-dispatch:-runtime_dispatches(repo,-inferred_methods(mod,-entry_frames(seeds,-mod)))","page":"Rules","text":"Pedantic. Calls the optimizer leaves to run-time dispatch in each frame: a :call of a generic function, or of Core._apply_iterate or Core.invoke. A logging macro's hand-off to the current logger is not reported. Pass the frames of entry_frames, so a @noinline callee reached only through an :invoke edge is read too. One site per method and source line.\n\nRepair: make the callee's argument types inferable, or put a function barrier around the untyped part. Opt out a deliberate barrier on the method's first line.","title":"runtime-dispatch: runtime_dispatches(repo, inferred_methods(mod, entry_frames(seeds, mod)))"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#widened-return:-widened_returns(repo,-inferred_methods(mod,-entry_frames(seeds,-mod)))","page":"Rules","text":"Pedantic. Methods whose inferred result a caller cannot compile against: anything but a concrete type, Union{}, a Type{X} constant, a union of at most four concrete types, or a fixed-length tuple of such members.\n\nRepair: make the result type depend only on the argument types.","title":"widened-return: widened_returns(repo, inferred_methods(mod, entry_frames(seeds, mod)))"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#float-widening:-float_widenings(repo,-inferred_methods(mod,-entry_frames(seeds,-mod)))","page":"Rules","text":"Pedantic. Statements whose float result is wider than every float the method receives in its arguments: x::Float32 * 2.0, n / m on Ints in a Float32 method, float(n), a Float64 global, or a returned 0.0. The detail names the operand that brings the wide float in (Base.Float64 for a conversion, 0.0, the global), or the callee. A value computed from an already widened one is not reported again. Methods with no float argument, or one already as wide as Float64, are skipped. Arguments count the floats they hold anywhere in their type (Vector{Float32}, Complex{Float16}).\n\nAt a runtime dispatch the rule lists the candidate methods (candidate_limit, as in unmarked-mutation). A candidate that returns a wider float makes the site definite. A dispatch with more candidates than the budget, or one inference cannot type, may widen: \"may widen (runtime-dispatch)\". A dispatch whose argument types cannot hold the method's floats is skipped.\n\nfloat64 finds the same literals and tokens in the source text of every method; this rule reads what the compiler made of them, for the argument types given. float64_ops counts the Float64 operations of one call.\n\nRepair: oftype(x, 2.0), T(0.5) or float(T)(n), with T the argument's float type.","title":"float-widening: float_widenings(repo, inferred_methods(mod, entry_frames(seeds, mod)))"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Anonymous-functions:-impure-anonymous-function,-unstable-anonymous-function,-overspecialized-anonymous-function","page":"Rules","text":"Three rules on anonymous functions (lambdas, do blocks and the generators of comprehensions) that capture variables; Julia calls these closures. One passes all three when it captures nothing (x -> x.field), or when every instance the package compiled captures only plain immutable data: non-function isbits values, Strings, Symbols, and immutable structs, tuples or small unions of them (x -> x * scale with scale::Float64). The rules read the compiled instances from Base.specializations, so they see what the package's precompile workload ran.\n\nRule Function Finds Repair\nimpure-anonymous-function impure_anonymous_functions(mod) a mutable capture (an array, Dict, Ref, a module); a Core.Box, a captured variable rebound; no compiled instance, so the captures are unverified pass the data as an argument, or use Base.Fix1/Base.Fix2 (filter(in(allowed), items)); cover an unverified function in the precompile workload\nunstable-anonymous-function unstable_anonymous_functions(mod) a capture whose type inference left abstract, or an instance built where the capture types are unknown make the captured variable's type concrete, or pass it as an argument\noverspecialized-anonymous-function overspecialized_anonymous_functions(mod) a captured type or function: the anonymous function compiles anew for every value pass it as an argument, or define a callable struct whose field is a DataType or Function","title":"Anonymous functions: impure-anonymous-function, unstable-anonymous-function, overspecialized-anonymous-function"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#abstract-field:-abstract_fields(type),-repeated-prefix:-repeated_prefix(type)","page":"Rules","text":"Both take a struct type. Apply them to every struct a module defines with module_structs(mod) and place each site with struct_site(name, struct_locations(files)).\n\nabstract_fields finds fields declared with an abstract type, or with a concrete container of one: Vector{Any}, Base.RefValue{Any} and Dict{Tuple, Any} are concrete, but every read from them is dynamically dispatched. Repair: make the field type a type parameter of the struct.\nrepeated_prefix finds field names that repeat a word the type should say once. Fields continuation_step and continuation_theta belong in a ContinuationControls.\n\nmutable-struct reports every struct of mutable_structs(mod). Repair: return the changed data from the function that computes it and keep the struct immutable. A struct that needs a finalizer, a cyclic reference or a lock's identity opts out with # lint: mutable-struct and a reason. A limit on field count (wide-struct) takes one line: fieldcount(T) > limit over module_structs(mod).\n\nfiles = repository_sources(REPO, (\"src\",))\nlocations = struct_locations(files)\nsites = [struct_site(nameof(T), locations) for T in module_structs(MyPackage) if !isempty(abstract_fields(T))]\nratchet!(REPO, \"abstract-field\", sites)","title":"abstract-field: abstract_fields(type), repeated-prefix: repeated_prefix(type)"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Rules-on-source-files","page":"Rules","text":"Each takes a file path and located_source(file), the parsed file.\n\nRule Function Finds Repair\nnothing-return nothing_returns declared Union{Nothing, …} results return a value that always means something, or throw\nrange-guard range_guards floatmin/floatmax, exp's range edges (88, 709), isfinite(exp(…)) compute in log space or clamp at the source\nrepeated-statement repeated_statements a statement repeated in one block; the same line in two branches passes delete the copy\nreturn-type return_type_calls calls of Core.Compiler.return_type, a guess at a result type restructure so the type is known\nconcrete-arg concrete_arguments arguments annotated Vector, Matrix, Array or Dict that the method never resizes AbstractVector{T} and the like; they accept views, OffsetArray and GPU arrays\nconcrete-return concrete_returns(file, located, mod) result types that name a concrete type, Vector{E} included; AbstractMatrix{T} passes; a constructor returning its own type is exempt annotate by what the arguments bind; Corset.CONCRETE_RETURN_FIX is the log text\nannotation missing_annotations methods with an unannotated argument or result annotate\nfloat64 float64_sites(file) Float64 tokens and untyped float literals; float-widening reads where they widen a narrower argument zero(T), T(0.5) or oftype(x, 0.5)\nref ref_sites(file) Ref and RefValue outside ccall, @ccall, cfunction, @cfunction and @ccallable Return the changed data from the function that computes it. A broadcast shield (f.(Ref(x), xs)) opts out with # lint: ref\nc-type c_type_sites(file) Cint, Cdouble and the other C-interop types outside ccall, @ccall, cfunction, @cfunction and @ccallable Int, Float64 or String; convert at the ccall\nfile-length long_file_sites(repo, file) source files longer than Repository.file_line_limit lines (default 1500) split the file by topic\none-letter one_letter_sites(repo, file) one-letter variable names (exempt: _ and Repository.one_letter_exempt) name the variable","title":"Rules on source files"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Rules-with-fixers","page":"Rules","text":"Two rules come with a function that repairs what they find.","title":"Rules with fixers"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#misplaced-import:-misplaced_imports(repo,-directories)","page":"Rules","text":"Imports that their file does not use, or that only other files of the module use. An import item belongs in the files that use its name. place_imports!(repo, directories) deletes the unused ones and moves the rest, and returns the sites it handled.","title":"misplaced-import: misplaced_imports(repo, directories)"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#where-return:-where_return_sites(file)","page":"Rules","text":"Short-form definitions whose where binds the return annotation:\n\nf(x::T)::T where {T} = x      # parses as f(x::T)::(T where {T}); T is not the method's T\n(f(x::T)::T) where {T} = x    # what was meant\n\nfix_where_returns! parenthesizes them.","title":"where-return: where_return_sites(file)"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Rules-that-call-other-tools","page":"Rules","text":"","title":"Rules that call other tools"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#fatou:-fatou_sites(repo,-directories)","page":"Rules","text":"One site per finding of Fatou's fatou lint, keyed by file and Fatou rule. fatou must be on PATH; the rule errors if it is not.","title":"fatou: fatou_sites(repo, directories)"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#jscpd:-jscpd_sites(repo,-directories)","page":"Rules","text":"One site per duplicate code block found by jscpd, keyed by the duplicate file and the duplicated file, placed at the duplicate block's lines. jscpd must be on PATH; the rule errors if it is not.","title":"jscpd: jscpd_sites(repo, directories)"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#jet:-[@call_sites](@ref),-[@opt_sites](@ref)","page":"Rules","text":"Reports of JET.@report_call and JET.@report_opt. See the guide.","title":"jet: @call_sites, @opt_sites"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#Command-Line-Interface","page":"CLI","text":"corset is the command-line tool for Corset.jl. It runs code-quality rules over a project's source and loaded package, judges findings against a baseline, prints formatted output, and optionally fixes or previews automated code rewrites.","title":"Command-Line Interface"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#Installation","page":"CLI","text":"Install corset using Julia's declarative application manager (Julia 1.13):\n\npkg> app add Corset\n\nYou can also run it via julia -m Corset:\n\njulia --project -m Corset check","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#Commands","page":"CLI","text":"","title":"Commands"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#corset-check","page":"CLI","text":"Run the configured rules over a project.\n\ncorset check [path] [options]\n\npath defaults to . (the current directory) and finds the project root at or above that path.","title":"corset check"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#Options","page":"CLI","text":"--format <format>: Output format (human, concise, or json). Default is human.\n--fix: Rewrite files in place for rules that provide an automated fixer (such as where-return and misplaced-import).\n--diff: Print a unified diff of the changes --fix would make without modifying any files on disk. Exits with code 1 if changes are detected, 0 if clean. Cannot be combined with --fix.\n--pedantic: Enable rules in the :pedantic group in addition to :default rules.\n--deny-warnings: Exit nonzero on warnings in addition to deny-level findings.\n--update-baseline: Seed missing baseline entries and lower counts for improved sites.\n--no-load: Skip loading the package module into Julia; runs only file and tree syntax rules.\n--candidate-limit <count>: The most candidate methods one runtime-dispatch site lists; 0 lists none. Overrides candidate_limit.\n--entries <sources>: Where the typed rules (abstract-local, bang, runtime-dispatch, unmarked-mutation, widened-return, float-widening) get their entry signatures, as a comma-separated list. workload (the default) takes the specializations the package's precompile workload compiled and the methods whose declared signature is already concrete. tests runs the package's tests under --trace-compile and keeps the traced signatures of the package's methods. none skips the typed rules. The command prints how many signatures each source gave and how many the walk inferred.\n--allow <rule>: Disable the specified rule (repeatable).\n--warn <rule>: Set the specified rule to warn (repeatable).\n--deny <rule>: Set the specified rule to deny (repeatable).","title":"Options"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#corset-rules","page":"CLI","text":"List all available rules, their group (default or pedantic), their configured level (allow, warn, or deny), and a one-line summary.\n\ncorset rules [path] [--pedantic]","title":"corset rules"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#Configuration","page":"CLI","text":"Settings are configured per-project in the [preferences.Corset] table of Project.toml, and can be overridden locally in LocalPreferences.toml under [Corset].\n\n[preferences.Corset]\ndirectories = [\"src\"]\nbaseline = \"code_baseline.toml\"\npedantic = false\nskipped_directories = [\"vendor\"]\none_letter_exempt = [\"p\", \"x\"]\ncandidate_limit = 4\nentry_points = \"test/entry_points.jl:signatures\"\n\n[preferences.Corset.levels]\nfloat64 = \"deny\"\nwhere-return = \"allow\"\n\nKeys:\n\ndirectories: Folders containing Julia source code to check (default: [\"src\"]).\nbaseline: Path to the baseline TOML file, relative to the project root.\npedantic: Boolean to enable all pedantic rules by default.\nskipped_directories: Directory names omitted wherever they sit.\none_letter_exempt: Variable names exempt from the one-letter rule.\nfile_line_limit: The most lines a source file may hold before the file-length rule reports it (default: 1500).\ncandidate_limit: The most methods unmarked-mutation and float-widening list at one runtime-dispatch site (default: 4; 0 lists none). A site with more methods keeps its conservative report. The budget is a count, so the findings do not depend on timing.\nentry_points: \"file.jl:function\", a file relative to the project root and a function in it that takes no arguments and returns a vector of signature types (Type[Tuple{typeof(MyPackage.f), Int}]). Its signatures replace the --entries sources.\nlevels: Map of rule names to :allow, :warn, or :deny.","title":"Configuration"},{"category":"section","location":"cli/#Exit-codes","page":"CLI","text":"0: Clean run (no deny-level findings, or no findings when --deny-warnings is set).\n1: One or more findings failed the run, or --diff detected rewrites.\n2: Usage error, invalid configuration, or execution failure.","title":"Exit codes"}]
}
